    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="0955" n="1789" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9128</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">DeBillier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-10T14:00:00-04:42">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Embassy’s March 6, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d885-f1"/> Chilean Government
                    studying status of officers and men of crew of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Seeadler</hi>. Appear inclined to regard them either as pirates or
                    shipwrecked sailors. As first view unlikely to prevail, danger they may escape
                    internment as crew of armed belligerent vessel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">DeBillier</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
